    <bf:title>
      <bf:Title>
	<bf:mainTitle>Boo! are you afraid of the dark?</bf:mainTitle>
      </bf:Title>
    </bf:title>
    <bf:content>
      <bf:Content rdf:about="http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/contentTypes/txt">
	<rdfs:label>text</rdfs:label>
	<bf:code>txt</bf:code>
      </bf:Content>
    </bf:content>
    <bf:summary>
      <bf:Summary>
	<rdfs:label>"A little boy's fear of the night becomes apparent to his mom when she walks into his room to find him hiding underneath the bed covers. She asks him if he is afraid of the dark and he instantly denies it. She knows that he is, so she says to him, "If I am afraid, can I hide under the covers with you?" When Boo's mom starts seeing and hearing scary things in the room, the little boy comes to her rescue and tries to ease her fear by identifying what is scaring her. The game Boo's mom decided to play with him in the story helps ease his fear of the dark and helped him work through those fears, by separating what was real from what is imaginary"-- Provided by publisher.</rdfs:label>
      </bf:Summary>
    </bf:summary>
    <bf:intendedAudience>
